    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1410">

                <pb facs="1517" n="1503" sameAs="frus:frus1944v07/pg1503"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.34112A/9–2244: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Paraguay</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Beaulac</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Asunción</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-09-22T16:00:00-04:00">September 22,
                            1944—4 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received September 23—12:36 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>537. The Minister for Foreign Affairs informed me this morning Paraguayan
                    Government is desirous of cooperating in sense of Department’s circular telegram
                    September 20, 5 p.m.<anchor n="80" xml:id="d1410-f1"/> I discussed with him in
                    principle possible absorption by Bank of Paraguay of Banco Germánico and forced
                    sale of spearhead Axis firms and he expressed a desire to discuss matters in
                    detail. I said if temporary financing were needed to carry out some of these
                    operations I should be glad to explore possibility of such financing by an
                    agency of our Government.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Beaulac</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
